{"author":{"id":"bc879001b271aeebdd38a690df6011bef3fd316a5680eda2689f43e26c43d0a4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795215390,"nonce":"6fUfNgR01waf8/ZHF2m2GkYy0rQ=","title":"A named relationship variable makes a MATCH return no rows","message":"At 64f41a2, naming the relationship in a pattern drops every row:\n\n- `MATCH (n:Npc)-[:Npc__KNOWS__Lore]-\u003e(l:Lore) RETURN l.id`: 2 rows (both edges).\n- `MATCH (n:Npc)-[e:Npc__KNOWS__Lore]-\u003e(l:Lore) RETURN l.id`: 0 rows.\n- `MATCH (n:Npc)-[e:Npc__KNOWS__Lore]-\u003e(l:Lore) RETURN l.id, e._hxn_revision`: 0 rows.\n\nThe edges were written through `apply_delta` with `UpsertEdge` carrying two properties (`_hxn_source STRING`, `_hxn_revision INT64`) on `CREATE REL TABLE Npc__KNOWS__Lore (FROM Npc TO Lore, _hxn_source STRING, _hxn_revision INT64)`. Edge properties therefore cannot be read by query. Found while testing hxn-assets' knowledge adapter; its tests count delta operations instead.","files":null}]}